WEBVTT

0
00:00.230 --> 00:01.930
<v Instructor>In this video, we're doing a couple examples</v>

1
00:01.930 --> 00:04.240
of how to simplify radical expressions,

2
00:04.240 --> 00:06.370
and just to clarify a few terms here,

3
00:06.370 --> 00:07.720
when we say an expression,

4
00:07.720 --> 00:09.400
we differentiate it from an equation

5
00:09.400 --> 00:11.550
because an equation has an equal sign, right,

6
00:11.550 --> 00:13.610
and there's two sides to the equal sign,

7
00:13.610 --> 00:15.800
the left-hand side of the equal sign and the right-hand side

8
00:15.800 --> 00:17.630
of the equal sign and that's an equation.

9
00:17.630 --> 00:19.630
An expression doesn't have an equal sign,

10
00:19.630 --> 00:21.420
so it's just an expression,

11
00:21.420 --> 00:24.180
it's not an equation, and we call it a radical expression

12
00:24.180 --> 00:27.150
because we have square roots involved or radicals involved.

13
00:27.150 --> 00:29.480
In this first problem, we have three times the square root

14
00:29.480 --> 00:32.080
of 2/7, minus five times the square root

15
00:32.080 --> 00:35.200
of 7/2 plus three times the square root of 56,

16
00:35.200 --> 00:38.200
and we want to simplify this radical expression.

17
00:38.200 --> 00:41.440
Doing so is just going to require us to know our rules

18
00:41.440 --> 00:42.950
of radical simplification.

19
00:42.950 --> 00:44.640
For example, one of the rules tells us

20
00:44.640 --> 00:47.000
that when we take the square root of a fraction,

21
00:47.000 --> 00:48.770
we can take the square root of the numerator

22
00:48.770 --> 00:50.380
and the denominator separately,

23
00:50.380 --> 00:52.380
which means that three times the square root

24
00:52.380 --> 00:55.080
of 2/7 becomes three times the square root

25
00:55.080 --> 00:57.499
of two over the square root of seven,

26
00:57.499 --> 00:59.265
and five times the square root

27
00:59.265 --> 01:01.370
of 7/2 becomes five times the square root

28
01:01.370 --> 01:03.590
of seven over the square root of two.

29
01:03.590 --> 01:06.910
Here, for the square root of 56, one thing

30
01:06.910 --> 01:09.810
that we can do is divide 56 by four

31
01:09.810 --> 01:11.240
and we can call this the square root

32
01:11.240 --> 01:13.520
of four times 14, right?

33
01:13.520 --> 01:15.050
We haven't changed this at all,

34
01:15.050 --> 01:18.320
because four times 14 is 56, so the square root

35
01:18.320 --> 01:22.320
of four times 14 is the same thing as the square root of 56.

36
01:22.320 --> 01:24.920
Now we want to go ahead and rationalize the denominators

37
01:24.920 --> 01:27.000
of both of these fractions here,

38
01:27.000 --> 01:27.840
which means that we just

39
01:27.840 --> 01:29.580
want to eliminate the square root

40
01:29.580 --> 01:30.870
from each of the denominators.

41
01:30.870 --> 01:33.280
In order to do that, we'll multiply the fraction

42
01:33.280 --> 01:35.510
by the denominator, so here we have the square root

43
01:35.510 --> 01:37.000
of two over the square root of seven,

44
01:37.000 --> 01:38.680
we want to multiply by the square root

45
01:38.680 --> 01:41.080
of seven over the square root of seven,

46
01:41.080 --> 01:43.590
because that'll make the denominator the square

47
01:43.590 --> 01:45.360
root of seven times the square root of seven,

48
01:45.360 --> 01:46.630
those square roots will cancel

49
01:46.630 --> 01:47.920
and we'll just be left with seven

50
01:47.920 --> 01:49.040
and we will have removed

51
01:49.040 --> 01:51.250
the square root from the denominator.

52
01:51.250 --> 01:52.083
Same thing here.

53
01:52.083 --> 01:52.970
We want to do the square root

54
01:52.970 --> 01:55.150
of two over the square root of two,

55
01:55.150 --> 01:57.880
and when we do that, we're going to get three times

56
01:57.880 --> 02:00.020
the square root of two times the square root of seven.

57
02:00.020 --> 02:01.810
Well, when we have the square root

58
02:01.810 --> 02:04.820
of m times the square root of n,

59
02:04.820 --> 02:08.060
that's the same thing as the square root of m n,

60
02:08.060 --> 02:10.060
and this is just radical multiplication.

61
02:10.060 --> 02:12.730
We know that when we have two radicals multiplied together,

62
02:12.730 --> 02:15.550
we can multiply the values that are inside the radicals,

63
02:15.550 --> 02:17.490
put it all under one radical sign,

64
02:17.490 --> 02:18.440
so here we have square root

65
02:18.440 --> 02:19.560
of two times square root of seven,

66
02:19.560 --> 02:20.720
that's going to become square root

67
02:20.720 --> 02:23.370
of 14 over square root of seven

68
02:23.370 --> 02:25.580
times square root of seven is just seven.

69
02:25.580 --> 02:27.840
Here we're going to have minus five times

70
02:27.840 --> 02:29.400
the square root of 14.

71
02:29.400 --> 02:31.950
We multiply root seven by root two,

72
02:31.950 --> 02:35.100
divided by root two times root two just gives us two,

73
02:35.100 --> 02:38.270
those radicals cancel, and then we're going to have plus three.

74
02:38.270 --> 02:39.370
Here we have the square root

75
02:39.370 --> 02:41.320
of four times 14, in other words,

76
02:41.320 --> 02:43.580
we have the square root of m times n.

77
02:43.580 --> 02:46.780
And if we just apply this formula backwards,

78
02:46.780 --> 02:48.490
we can see that we can separate m

79
02:48.490 --> 02:50.180
and n into their own square roots,

80
02:50.180 --> 02:53.290
which means we can separate root four times 14

81
02:53.290 --> 02:56.870
into root four times root 14 like this.

82
02:56.870 --> 02:59.360
Now, we know that the square root of four is two,

83
02:59.360 --> 03:01.350
so instead of four, we can call this two,

84
03:01.350 --> 03:03.620
and two times three gives us six,

85
03:03.620 --> 03:07.760
so we'll replace this three root four here with six

86
03:07.760 --> 03:10.280
and now we have plus six times the square root of 14.

87
03:10.280 --> 03:12.160
Notice now that we have just square root

88
03:12.160 --> 03:13.710
of 14, square root of 14

89
03:13.710 --> 03:16.270
and square root of 14, so our goal is going to be

90
03:16.270 --> 03:18.880
to combine these into one term.

91
03:18.880 --> 03:19.713
The way that we're going to do

92
03:19.713 --> 03:21.960
that is by finding a common denominator.

93
03:21.960 --> 03:26.410
We essentially have here 3/7 times root 14

94
03:26.410 --> 03:31.410
minus 5/2 times root 14 plus 6/1 times root 14.

95
03:34.060 --> 03:36.340
So what we want to do is find the common denominator,

96
03:36.340 --> 03:37.570
which means we need the least common

97
03:37.570 --> 03:39.870
multiple of seven, two, and one.

98
03:39.870 --> 03:42.720
That's going to be 14, so we're going to multiply

99
03:42.720 --> 03:46.160
this first fraction by 2/2.

100
03:46.160 --> 03:48.453
We're going to multiply this fraction by 7/7,

101
03:49.320 --> 03:53.490
and we're going to multiply here by 14/14.

102
03:53.490 --> 03:58.490
And when we do that, we're going to get 6/14 times root 14,

103
03:58.620 --> 04:03.620
minus 35/14 times root 14 plus 14 times six is 60

104
04:05.610 --> 04:10.610
and 24, 84/14 times root 14.

105
04:10.620 --> 04:13.990
Now I just need to find six minus 35 plus 84.

106
04:13.990 --> 04:16.010
If I combine my positive terms first,

107
04:16.010 --> 04:18.000
six plus 84 gives me 90.

108
04:18.000 --> 04:22.170
90 minus 35 gives me 55, so what I'm going to end up with

109
04:22.170 --> 04:27.000
is 55/14 times root 14,

110
04:27.000 --> 04:29.830
and I know that I can't reduce this fraction any further

111
04:29.830 --> 04:32.830
because the only factors of 14 other than one are two,

112
04:32.830 --> 04:35.010
seven, and 14, and two,

113
04:35.010 --> 04:38.560
seven, and 14, none of those go evenly into 55,

114
04:38.560 --> 04:43.560
so 55/14 times root 14 is going to be our final answer.

115
04:44.480 --> 04:46.050
Now let's look at a second example.

116
04:46.050 --> 04:47.600
Here we have the third root

117
04:47.600 --> 04:50.660
of x to the fifth y cubed times

118
04:50.660 --> 04:53.440
the fourth root of x y to the fifth.

119
04:53.440 --> 04:55.830
Now, remember the exponent on each of these variables,

120
04:55.830 --> 04:57.340
for example here x to the fifth,

121
04:57.340 --> 04:58.950
the five is the exponent,

122
04:58.950 --> 05:02.020
the three is the root, so this is the same thing as saying x

123
05:02.020 --> 05:04.700
to the fifth and then raised again to the 1/3 power.

124
05:04.700 --> 05:05.720
So what we're going to do is

125
05:05.720 --> 05:08.120
we're going to take this value inside the square root here,

126
05:08.120 --> 05:10.250
x to the fifth y to the 1/3,

127
05:10.250 --> 05:12.800
and we're going to take the 1/3 root like this.

128
05:12.800 --> 05:13.840
We haven't changed anything.

129
05:13.840 --> 05:16.050
We can write the 1/3 root as the 1/3 root

130
05:16.050 --> 05:17.580
of x to the fifth y to the third

131
05:17.580 --> 05:18.890
like in the original problem,

132
05:18.890 --> 05:20.380
or take what's inside the square root

133
05:20.380 --> 05:21.850
and raise it to the 1/3 power.

134
05:21.850 --> 05:23.050
So those things are the same.

135
05:23.050 --> 05:26.350
And same thing here, we can take x y to the fifth

136
05:26.350 --> 05:29.050
and raise it to the 1/4 instead.

137
05:29.050 --> 05:30.740
Now what we can do is distribute

138
05:30.740 --> 05:34.220
this 1/3 exponent across the five and the three.

139
05:34.220 --> 05:36.330
When we do that, we multiply our exponents,

140
05:36.330 --> 05:40.850
so five times 1/3 is 5/3, so we get x to the 5/3,

141
05:40.850 --> 05:44.320
and then y to the 1/3 to the 1/3 again is y

142
05:44.320 --> 05:49.320
to the three times 1/3 or just y to the 3/3.

143
05:49.440 --> 05:53.450
Here, we're going to have x to the 1/4, so x to the 1/4,

144
05:53.450 --> 05:55.910
and then y to the 1/5 raised to the 1/4 again.

145
05:55.910 --> 06:00.280
We multiply five and 1/4 and we get y to the 5/4.

146
06:00.280 --> 06:02.370
And now we know from the rules of exponents,

147
06:02.370 --> 06:03.670
remember we know that x

148
06:03.670 --> 06:08.670
to the a times x to the b is equal to x to the a plus b.

149
06:09.090 --> 06:10.570
This is exponent addition here.

150
06:10.570 --> 06:12.110
We add the exponents.

151
06:12.110 --> 06:13.730
So because we have the same bases here,

152
06:13.730 --> 06:16.850
x to the 5/3 and x to the 1/4, we can say x

153
06:16.850 --> 06:21.060
to the 5/3 plus 1/4 and for y here,

154
06:21.060 --> 06:23.700
we have y to the 3/3, which is the same thing as y

155
06:23.700 --> 06:25.150
to the one, and then we have y

156
06:25.150 --> 06:30.150
to the 5/4, so we can say times y to the one plus 5/4.

157
06:30.410 --> 06:33.000
Now it's just a matter of finding a common denominator

158
06:33.000 --> 06:34.580
between our fractions here,

159
06:34.580 --> 06:36.550
so the common denominator for 5/3

160
06:36.550 --> 06:38.930
and 1/4 is going to be 12,

161
06:38.930 --> 06:43.270
so we're going to say 4/4, we're going to multiply by 4/4, here

162
06:43.270 --> 06:45.600
we're going to multiply by 3/3.

163
06:45.600 --> 06:49.110
The common denominator for one and 5/4 is going to be four,

164
06:49.110 --> 06:52.079
so we're going to multiply this one by 4/4

165
06:52.079 --> 06:54.160
which is just going to give us 4/4.

166
06:54.160 --> 06:56.430
And now we just need to combine exponents,

167
06:56.430 --> 06:58.150
so for x, we're going to get x

168
06:58.150 --> 07:03.150
to the 20/12 plus 3/12 times y to the 9/4.

169
07:06.350 --> 07:07.630
when we add 20 to three,

170
07:07.630 --> 07:10.810
we're going to get 23, so our final answer is going to be x

171
07:10.810 --> 07:15.810
to the 23/12 times y to the 9/4,

172
07:16.010 --> 07:17.920
and even though it looks completely different,

173
07:17.920 --> 07:20.720
we just used the rules that we knew about exponents

174
07:20.720 --> 07:23.010
and radicals or roots to change

175
07:23.010 --> 07:25.960
this original problem into our final answer here

176
07:25.960 --> 07:29.080
and they actually mean exactly the same thing.

177
07:29.080 --> 07:30.660
Let's do one final example here.

178
07:30.660 --> 07:34.800
We have the third root of 27 times the square root of three.

179
07:34.800 --> 07:36.660
Using our formula here where we have the square root

180
07:36.660 --> 07:37.780
of m times the square root

181
07:37.780 --> 07:40.530
of n is equal to the square root of m n,

182
07:40.530 --> 07:42.070
here we basically have m

183
07:42.070 --> 07:46.150
and n where m is 27 and n is the square root of three.

184
07:46.150 --> 07:49.090
We know we can separate those into their own square roots,

185
07:49.090 --> 07:50.890
so we can say that the third root

186
07:50.890 --> 07:55.520
of 27 times the third root of the square root of three.

187
07:55.520 --> 07:56.353
Keep in mind that we know

188
07:56.353 --> 07:59.750
that 27 is three times three times three, right?

189
07:59.750 --> 08:01.190
Three times three is nine.

190
08:01.190 --> 08:03.720
Nine times three is 27, so 27 is equal

191
08:03.720 --> 08:06.640
to three to the third, so we can say the third root

192
08:06.640 --> 08:09.480
of three to the third and then here

193
08:09.480 --> 08:11.260
we're going to say the third root of

194
08:11.260 --> 08:12.770
and we're going to change the square root

195
08:12.770 --> 08:16.930
of three to three to the 1/2, like this.

196
08:16.930 --> 08:19.200
Now we can do the same thing we did in the last example,

197
08:19.200 --> 08:22.120
so this three to the third inside the square root,

198
08:22.120 --> 08:23.810
instead of taking the third root here,

199
08:23.810 --> 08:25.620
we raise it to the 1/3 power,

200
08:25.620 --> 08:28.310
then we take three to the 1/2,

201
08:28.310 --> 08:30.430
and instead of taking the third root here,

202
08:30.430 --> 08:32.170
we raise it to the 1/3 power.

203
08:32.170 --> 08:34.010
Now this is exponent multiplication,

204
08:34.010 --> 08:38.440
so three times 1/3 is going to be 3/3, so we get three

205
08:38.440 --> 08:42.355
to the 3/3, and then we're going to say 1/2 times 1/3

206
08:42.355 --> 08:45.540
is 1/6, so we get three to the 1/6,

207
08:45.540 --> 08:46.610
and now it's back to this

208
08:46.610 --> 08:49.060
formula up here of exponent addition.

209
08:49.060 --> 08:50.990
So we're going to call this 3/3, we're just going to call

210
08:50.990 --> 08:55.970
that one, and we're going to say three to the one plus 1/6.

211
08:55.970 --> 08:57.770
If we find a common denominator,

212
08:57.770 --> 09:01.350
we have to multiply this one by 6/6,

213
09:01.350 --> 09:03.760
and now we can say six plus one is seven,

214
09:03.760 --> 09:06.770
so we get three to the 7/6,

215
09:06.770 --> 09:10.260
which is going to be the same thing as this original problem

216
09:10.260 --> 09:11.430
that we started with up here.

217
09:11.430 --> 09:13.720
We just used exponent rules

218
09:13.720 --> 09:18.720
and radical rules to simplify it to three to the 7/6.